n. Clicking a quick button clears the custom field and makes that percentage active again. Results update on every keystroke and click, and all amounts come from the existing `tip.js`, shown with exactly two decimals.\n- **Invalid input:** while anything is invalid, the field is marked invalid for screen readers (`aria-invalid`), its message is shown, and all three results show the dash. Old numbers never stay on screen.\n- **Layout:** built for phones first. The content column is capped at 30rem wide on desktop. Every control is at least 44×44px, there are visible keyboard-focus outlines, and the quick buttons sit in a three-column grid that shrinks to fit. The selected button changes colour and also gets an inner ring and underline, so selection isn't shown by colour alone.\n\n**Decisions you might want to change:**\n- **Bill error on load:** the bill message (\"Enter a bill amount greater than 0\") shows as soon as the page loads, because the bill starts empty. I did this so every invalid field always has its message, but you may prefer to hide it until the user types.\n- **Emptying the custom field:** this leaves no tip selected, so the custom field shows \"Enter a tip percentage of 0 or more\" rather than falling back to a quick tip.\n\n`test/app.test.js` covers the selection logic, the two worked examples (100 / 15% / 3 → 15.00, 115.00, 38.34 and 50 / 20% / 2 → 10.00, 60.00, 30.00), the dashes on invalid input, and checks on the markup and styles. I couldn't run the page in a browser, so the 360px no-horizontal-scroll check rests on the CSS alone.\n\nTo check it, run these from the worktree:\n```\nnode --test\nnode --check app.js\nnode --check tip.js\n```\nThen run the `grep` and `test -f` gates for WU-002 listed in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.","ttft_ms":5196,"type":"result","duration_ms":121536,"uuid":"99c6f973-630b-4823-8dc0-e7615a630cf0","ttft_stream_ms":4715,"time_to_request_ms":3966,"first_content_frame_ms":4716,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

